  "summary": "Package fetches and executes remote scripts from a mutable Bitbucket branch",
  "details": "The package's main module fetches HTML from https://bitbucket.org/p2p-alt-public/p2p-emis/raw/main/GameWebSight, replaces the host page's head and body with the parsed remote document, and re-creates <script> elements so the remote JavaScript executes in the consuming page. The source is a mutable `main` branch on a third-party repository, so whoever controls that repo can change the executed payload at any time without republishing the npm package. Package metadata is minimal (empty author, one-line description 'Website loader for remote HTML content') and the module has no other functionality — its sole behavior is loading and executing remote code.",
